/ The history section under the live table: connections that ended in
/ the selected window (ClosedConnection), newest first, rollup counter
/ rows rendered as one collapsed line. The teardown that writes a row
/ here also triggers a refresh broadcast, so a closing connection moves
/ from the live table to here within one refresh.
section.mt-4.rounded-lg.border.border-slate-200.dark:border-slate-800.bg-white.dark:bg-slate-900
  header.border-b.border-slate-200.dark:border-slate-800.px-4.py-3
    h2.font-semibold Recent connections
    p.text-sm.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
      ' Connections that ended in the selected window, newest first.
      ' Anonymous noise past #{MailOnRails::ClosedConnection.max_rows_per_ip} rows per
      ' address and hour is collapsed into one counter row; authenticated
      ' connections are always kept individually.
  - if @history.any?
    / No overflow container, like the live table above: cells compress
    / and long mono values break, so nothing scrolls but the page.
    table.w-full.text-sm
      thead.text-left.text-xs.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
        tr
          th.px-4.py-2 Address
          th.px-4.py-2 Listener
          th.px-4.py-2 TLS
          th.px-4.py-2 User
          - if controller_name == "smtp"
            th.px-4.py-2 HELO
            th.px-4.py-2.text-right Messages
          - else
            th.px-4.py-2 State
          th.px-4.py-2.text-right Duration
          th.px-4.py-2.text-right Tarpit
          th.px-4.py-2 Closed
          th.px-4.py-2
      tbody
        - @history.each do |row|
          tr.border-t.border-slate-100.dark:border-slate-800
            - if row.rollup?
              td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
                = row.ip
                = render "ip_meta", ip: row.ip
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400 colspan=(controller_name == "smtp" ? 8 : 7)
                = "#{number_with_delimiter(row.connection_count)} connections collapsed (hour starting #{row.closed_at.strftime("%b %-d %H:%M")})"
            - else
              td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all
                = row.ip || "?"
                = render "ip_meta", ip: row.ip
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300
                = row.port
                - if row.role
                  span.ml-1.text-xs.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400= row.role
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= row.tls? ? "✓" : "-"
              td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all= row.username || "-"
              - if controller_name == "smtp"
                td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= row.helo || "-"
                td.px-4.py-1.5.text-right.tabular-nums.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= row.messages || "-"
              - else
                td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= row.final_state || "-"
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-right.tabular-nums.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= duration_label(row.duration_seconds)
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-right.tabular-nums class=(row.tarpit_seconds ? "text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400" : "text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300")
                = row.tarpit_seconds ? duration_label(row.tarpit_seconds) : "-"
              td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= row.closed_at.strftime("%b %-d %H:%M")
            td.px-4.py-1.5.text-right
              / Captured dialogue of an abnormally ended session
              / (smtp_trace_capture).
              - if !row.rollup? && row.transcript_id
                = link_to "Transcript", session_transcript_path(row.transcript_id), class: "mr-2 text-xs font-medium text-accent hover:underline"
              - if row.ip
                = render "auth_attempts/ban_button", target: row.ip, origin: controller_name, confirm: "Ban #{row.ip}? Its live connections are dropped and it loses SMTP, IMAP and web login access."
  - else
    p.px-4.py-3.text-sm.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400 Nothing in this window.
